<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<SActionScript version="1" name="fader_post_fx">

  <!-- Proposal 37 P3a (design D5): THE TRACK FADER IS POST-FX.

       Until this phase the fader was a per-page scalar inside
       twTrackMix::freezePage_nolock, i.e. applied BEFORE the inserts (design
       F6). It is now twGainStage, wired between the plugin chain and the
       rewire:

           twTrackMix -> twPluginChain -> twGainStage -> twRewire

       WHY THIS CASE EXISTS AT ALL. The move cannot be gated by a byte compare:
       no committed golden combines a non-unity fader with a plugin (verified by
       reading tests/goldens/mc_{mono,stereo}.qxp - every `volume=` in both is
       '0'), so every golden renders identically across the move BY
       CONSTRUCTION, which proves nothing about the ordering. And a LINEAR
       insert cannot tell the two orders apart either: gain and fader commute.
       So the ordering is gated here, twice.

       (a) VALUE. A -6.02 dB fader and tw.test.clap.gain at 2.0 must still
           multiply out to unity, and the fader must still be in the metered
           path. This is the half of the behaviour that must NOT change.

       (b) ORDER. A -6.02 dB fader and a HARD CLIPPER (tw.test.clap.gain's
           "Clip Threshold", param id 2 - see tw303a/plugins/tests/twtestclap.c;
           the clipper runs after the plugin's own gain, which is left at 1.0).
           Clipping does not commute with a scalar, so the two orders give
           different audio, and the fixture is chosen to put the threshold
           BETWEEN them:

               pre-FX  (the OLD order):  fader first  -> peak 0.475 < 0.5,
                                         the clipper never engages
                                         -> rms = 0.5 * rms(source)
               post-FX (the NEW order):  clipper first -> the 0.95-peak
                                         sawtooth is clipped, THEN halved
                                         -> a strictly lower rms

       THE FIXTURE, and the closed form. ../test_clipsaw.wav (written by
       tests/tools/gen_clip_fixture.py, which prints these numbers): 2.0 s,
       48 kHz, 16-bit, a 100 Hz sawtooth of amplitude 0.95 - 480 samples per
       period, so 480 divides 48000 exactly and EVERY one-second window has the
       same rms. Computed over the fixture's own samples (x = int16/32768):

           peak                             0.949982
           rms, one second                  0.548468
           pre-FX  0.5 * rms                0.274234     <- the old order
           post-FX 0.5 * rms(clip(x, 0.5))  0.201419     <- the new order

       The +/-1 % band around 0.201419 is [0.199405, 0.203433], which is 26 %
       away from 0.274234 - so this case FAILS on a pre-move binary, and it was
       verified to do so once (recorded in plan/STATE.md, 2026-08-16).

       LAYOUT. Two tracks in DISJOINT time windows so one render answers both
       questions and a byte offset attributes a difference to a path by itself
       (the same discipline tools/gen_mc_corpus.qxa uses):

           0.0 - 4.0 s   track 0   ../test_sawtooth.wav  + gain 2.0
           4.0 - 6.0 s   track 1   ../test_clipsaw.wav   + clip 0.5

       -6.0206 dB, not -6.02: it is 0.4999995, i.e. exactly half to seven
       digits, which is what makes the +/-1 % bands honest. -->

  <setup project="new"/>

  <actions>
    <add-track index="-1"/>
    <add-track index="-1"/>

    <set-track-volume trackIndex="0" volume="-6.0206"/>
    <set-track-volume trackIndex="1" volume="-6.0206"/>

    <add-sample trackIndex="0" filePath="../test_sawtooth.wav" timePos="0"/>
    <add-sample trackIndex="1" filePath="../test_clipsaw.wav" timePos="192000"/>

    <!-- (a) a plain gain of 2.0 ... -->
    <insert-plugin trackPath="0" slotIndex="0" format="clap"
                   uid="tw.test.clap.gain" name="Test Gain" vendor="Smaragd"
                   path="twtestclap.clap" nIn="2" nOut="2"/>
    <set-plugin-param trackPath="0" slotIndex="0" paramId="0" value="2.0"/>

    <!-- (b) ... and a clipper at 0.5, with the plugin's own gain left at 1.0. -->
    <insert-plugin trackPath="1" slotIndex="0" format="clap"
                   uid="tw.test.clap.gain" name="Test Gain" vendor="Smaragd"
                   path="twtestclap.clap" nIn="2" nOut="2"/>
    <set-plugin-param trackPath="1" slotIndex="0" paramId="2" value="0.5"/>

    <render filename="fpf_main.wav" format="wav" quality="10" durationSec="6.0"/>

    <!-- (a) VALUE: 0.5 * 2.0 = 1.0, so the first second of test_sawtooth.wav
         comes back at its unprocessed rms of 0.066650. +/-1 % = [0.065984,
         0.067317]; widened by a hair on each side for the 16-bit round trip. -->
    <assert-audio-energy filename="fpf_main.wav"
                         startFrame="0" frameCount="48000"
                         channel="0" minRms="0.06598" maxRms="0.06732"/>

    <!-- (b) ORDER: the clipper saw the UNFADED signal. 0.201419 +/-1 %.
         The old, pre-FX order lands on 0.274234 and fails this band. -->
    <assert-audio-energy filename="fpf_main.wav"
                         startFrame="192000" frameCount="48000"
                         channel="0" minRms="0.19940" maxRms="0.20344"/>

    <!-- (a) continued: THE METER, at 0.5 s, reads the post-fader post-FX level.
         twLevelProbe measures the 256-frame window ending at the position, and
         over [23744, 24000) the raw fixture's rms is 0.058928. The fader and the
         plugin are the only two things in the path, and they cancel - so this
         band (+/-15 %) is passed ONLY if BOTH are in it: the plugin alone would
         read 0.1179 and the fader alone 0.0295, and both are far outside. -->
    <assert-meter trackIndex="0" position="24000"
                  minRms="0.05010" maxRms="0.06780"/>

    <!-- (a) continued: bypass the insert and the fader alone remains, so the
         first second halves to 0.033325. +/-1 % = [0.032992, 0.033658]. -->
    <set-plugin-bypass trackPath="0" slotIndex="0" bypassed="true"/>

    <render filename="fpf_bypassed.wav" format="wav" quality="10" durationSec="6.0"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="fpf_bypassed.wav"
                         startFrame="0" frameCount="48000"
                         channel="0" minRms="0.03293" maxRms="0.03372"/>

    <!-- ...and track 1, untouched, must not have moved. -->
    <assert-audio-energy filename="fpf_bypassed.wav"
                         startFrame="192000" frameCount="48000"
                         channel="0" minRms="0.19940" maxRms="0.20344"/>

    <!-- The bypass undoes exactly, which also re-proves that a chain edit made
         after a position was first rendered reaches the render. -->
    <undo count="1"/>

    <render filename="fpf_undone.wav" format="wav" quality="10" durationSec="6.0"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="fpf_undone.wav"
                         startFrame="0" frameCount="48000"
                         channel="0" minRms="0.06598" maxRms="0.06732"/>
  </actions>

  <assertions>
    <assert-track-count equals="2"/>
  </assertions>

</SActionScript>
